<p>An improvement that would provide a large benefit to Astorians is the implementation of CBTC on these two lines.</p>

<h2 id="what-is-cbtc">What is CBTC</h2>
<p>Communications-based train control, or CBTC, is a railway signaling system that uses telecommuniciations to provide a more accurate location of the train compared to the automatic block signaling, or ABS, system currently used. The ABS system divides the track into a series of blocks and the signaling system could detect whether blocks are occupied or available and automatically determine whether the train can proceed to the future blocks. CBTC is a continuous system, so it can detect train positions more accurately, reducing headways and delays, providing more accurate arrival time estimates, and increasing safety.</p>

<h2 id="prioritizing-cbtc">Prioritizing CBTC</h2>
<p>When discussing improvements, it makes sense to consider improving entire lines together. This will then need to be further broken down by station, track lines, rolling stock, etc.</p>

